Z||000008||sombre||05-09-2001||11:32 PM||||As long as it's line level no speaker level it should be fine.Should not boost the power or feedback...It will be true mono not center channel,but from what I have seen on the subject that is what the idea is.To give a low level of sound just to add some depth from the rear.This will also work up front though not as well as true center.<P>  I did pretty much the same thing with an EQ but for different reasons when I competed in my camaro. I used an alpine 3331 in the dash so I had easy controll and it had a 12 db boost for the sub channel.I ran in the 0-100 watt class so I only had 1 amp running fronts and rears and annother 2 channel on the subs.<P>  I came out of the eq using the front outs and the sub outs the y-ed them together right  subto right front left sub to left front.One set of RCAs to the back then through a 2 channel 31 band eq then split again with y's at the crossover...Ran this way for 2 years and netted as high as 2nd at a regional event.Never did hear a down side other than shops saying I should split it and buy 2 of eveything to keep controll over each channel seperatly...Sounded fine to me with the controll I had.<BR>                             Greg||||reg||1
Z||000009||TOM||05-09-2001||11:43 PM||||Because the interior of a fiero is SOOOO big that you have dead spots that NEED a fill?||||reg||1
